---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
---

<section class="sec" id="big">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rv">
      <div class="label">Big work</div>
      <h2 class="h2">Big features: plan first, then build in pieces.</h2>
      <p class="sub">
        Two things Otaq does for a feature that’s too big for one sitting. Both are stages in a flow, so they
        show up on the board like everything else.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="big rv">
      <div class="half">
        <h3>Plan it first</h3>
        <p>
          With the <b>Spec first</b> preset, planning is stages. An agent asks you one question at a time and
          commits each decision to your project’s docs. Another works out how. A third writes the plan as
          numbered pieces. You check all three at <b>Spec review</b>, then Dev starts. Small tickets skip the
          planning stages.
        </p>
        <div class="shot">
          <div class="bar">
            <span class="pill p-w">
              <Icon icon="activity" />
              Product spec
            </span>
            <b>SHOP-40</b>Wishlist
            <span style="margin-left:auto">
              <span class="av av-CC">CC</span> Spec writer
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="bd qa">
            <div class="q">
              <span class="who">Spec writer · question 3 of 5</span>Should a signed-out visitor be able to add
              to a wishlist, or do we ask them to sign in first?
              <div class="o" style="margin-top:8px">
                <span class="pick">Ask them to sign in</span>
                <span>Keep a local wishlist, merge on sign-in</span>
                <span>Other…</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="a">Ask them to sign in. Keep it simple for v1.</div>
            <div class="dec">
              <Icon icon="lightbulb" class="s13" />
              <span>
                <b>Decision 3, committed to docs/decisions:</b> wishlist needs a signed-in user.
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="plan" style="margin-top:6px">
              <div class="ph">Plan · 4 pieces · written by Milestone plan</div>
              <div class="pr">
                <span class="n">1</span>Wishlist API<span class="s"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="pr">
                <span class="n">2</span>Wishlist button<span class="s">waits for 1</span>
              </div>
              <div class="pr">
                <span class="n">3</span>Wishlist page<span class="s">waits for 1</span>
              </div>
              <div class="pr">
                <span class="n">4</span>Share link<span class="s">waits for 2, 3</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="half">
        <h3>Build it in pieces</h3>
        <p>
          A big ticket stays <b>one card</b>. Its build agent, the one in charge, starts a helper agent per
          piece, each in its own worktree, and merges their work. The helpers show as rows inside the card. A
          helper’s question goes to the agent in charge first; only what it can’t settle reaches you. The
          checks judge the whole ticket, and it takes one slot of your agent limit.
        </p>
        <div class="shot">
          <div class="bar">
            <span class="pill p-w">
              <Icon icon="loader" class="spin" />
              Dev
            </span>
            <span style="color: var(--text-muted)">One card, four worktrees</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bd">
            <div class="bigcard attn">
              <div class="k">
                SHOP-40 · Wishlist<span class="av av-CC">CC</span>
              </div>
              <div class="ti">Wishlist</div>
              <div class="st">40.2 asks: keep the heart filled after sign-out?</div>
              <div class="plan">
                <div class="ph">Pieces · 4</div>
                <div class="pr">
                  <span class="n">40.1</span>Wishlist API<span class="s ok">merged</span>
                </div>
                <div class="pr">
                  <span class="n">40.2</span>Wishlist button<span class="s a">asks you</span>
                </div>
                <div class="pr">
                  <span class="n">40.3</span>Wishlist page<span class="s r">being reviewed</span>
                </div>
                <div class="pr">
                  <span class="n">40.4</span>Share link<span class="s">waits for 40.2, 40.3</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--text-muted)">
                <span class="av av-CC">CC</span>Rust developer · in charge
                <span class="btn btn-p btn-sm ans" style="margin-left:auto;height:24px;font-size:12px">
                  Answer
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
